{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00211",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 4.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Hello there. Please, sit. You came on your own today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.92,
      "end_seconds": 9.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Well, you know, yes, I managed on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.55,
      "end_seconds": 12.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Right, what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.78,
      "end_seconds": 17.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Honestly, it's palpitations, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.53,
      "end_seconds": 22.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "And when did that start? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.16,
      "end_seconds": 30.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "It's, It's been two months, I'm fairly sure. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.0,
      "end_seconds": 38.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.56,
      "end_seconds": 48.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly. Honestly, a few times a day. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.42,
      "end_seconds": 52.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.04,
      "end_seconds": 57.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get lightheadedness as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.31,
      "end_seconds": 61.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Has there been shortness of breath with it too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.21,
      "end_seconds": 65.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.13,
      "end_seconds": 69.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.27,
      "end_seconds": 75.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Okay, so about a eight out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.66,
      "end_seconds": 79.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Have you had palpitations before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.36,
      "end_seconds": 84.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.96,
      "end_seconds": 86.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.37,
      "end_seconds": 89.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Not at all, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.1,
      "end_seconds": 93.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Any fainting or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.86,
      "end_seconds": 95.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.82,
      "end_seconds": 99.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Any leg swelling, tremor or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.79,
      "end_seconds": 105.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Right, I haven't had leg swelling, tremor or fever, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.13,
      "end_seconds": 109.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.36,
      "end_seconds": 116.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I mean, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.64,
      "end_seconds": 120.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Alright, I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.41,
      "end_seconds": 122.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.17,
      "end_seconds": 142.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Do you have any known allergies at all? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.82,
      "end_seconds": 150.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Penicillin. I come out in... well, hives. Yes, sulfa drugs, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.7,
      "end_seconds": 157.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.57,
      "end_seconds": 163.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "I'm, I'm on Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 165.07,
      "end_seconds": 169.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 micrograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.07,
      "end_seconds": 173.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.2,
      "end_seconds": 177.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.53,
      "end_seconds": 180.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.4,
      "end_seconds": 183.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.03,
      "end_seconds": 186.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.3,
      "end_seconds": 191.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.77,
      "end_seconds": 195.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Okay, did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.66,
      "end_seconds": 199.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.22,
      "end_seconds": 207.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.31,
      "end_seconds": 223.12,
      "duration_seconds": 14.81,
      "text": "I've, I've got anxiety. I've got an underactive thyroid. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.91,
      "end_seconds": 230.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Alright. Yes, I can see the an underactive thyroid in your file as well. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.64,
      "end_seconds": 233.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.92,
      "end_seconds": 239.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.19,
      "end_seconds": 242.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 243.39,
      "end_seconds": 251.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 110, temperature 36.6, respiratory rate 16, weight 53 kilos, height 172 centimetres, pressure 133 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.54,
      "end_seconds": 256.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.1,
      "end_seconds": 269.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "Well, yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.39,
      "end_seconds": 275.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.63,
      "end_seconds": 278.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.83,
      "end_seconds": 298.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "No murmurs and the neck veins aren't distended."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.11,
      "end_seconds": 300.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.45,
      "end_seconds": 304.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.91,
      "end_seconds": 314.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Pulse is irregular right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.7,
      "end_seconds": 340.91,
      "duration_seconds": 21.21,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep a thyroid problem in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.3,
      "end_seconds": 346.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.22,
      "end_seconds": 362.69,
      "duration_seconds": 15.47,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had palpitations for two months, moderate, and no fainting or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.17,
      "end_seconds": 367.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Um, uh, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.49,
      "end_seconds": 372.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.14,
      "end_seconds": 373.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.21,
      "end_seconds": 395.66,
      "duration_seconds": 14.45,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Let's get a thyroid test, for palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'd like to arrange a Holter monitor for palpitations. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 396.54,
      "end_seconds": 399.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I've already done an ECG, it's ready for you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.2,
      "end_seconds": 427.76,
      "duration_seconds": 26.56,
      "text": "Okay, thanks, I'll look at that. Let's use metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. That should help with palpitations. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.96,
      "end_seconds": 441.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.11,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.96,
      "end_seconds": 443.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.19,
      "end_seconds": 458.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you faint or have chest pain with the racing. Let's review you in two weeks. Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.46,
      "end_seconds": 467.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "So, I take the metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.89,
      "end_seconds": 473.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Alright, yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 475.16,
      "end_seconds": 478.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Thanks so much, um, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 479.17,
      "end_seconds": 479.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}